Revision 01;
Designer decpld;
Company  decpld;
Assembly none;
Location none;
Device   g22v10;

/* SPEC.md 7.4, output enable: `Y.OE = E`.

   The one control this project has never measured. `ioin14`..`ioin23`
   showed an undriven I/O pin leaving its output-enable row entirely
   intact, and the claim that the OE ROW is what holds the pin off is an
   INFERENCE from it being the only remaining control in the fuse map --
   not a measurement. This design drives the enable from a pin, so the
   row must carry that pin's literal, at an address this experiment
   reads directly.

   Held constant against `oe-always`: same data term, same pins, same
   macrocell. Only the enable expression varies. */

PIN 2  = i0;
PIN 3  = e;
PIN 23 = o0;

o0    = i0;
o0.oe = e;
